# Optional. Copy to /etc/ai-diary/frontend.env on the Pi (no secrets belong here; the OpenAI key is backend-only):
#   sudo install -m 0640 -o root -g ai-diary frontend.env.example /etc/ai-diary/frontend.env
# Read by the FRONTEND unit only.
#
# Default: the UI binds 127.0.0.1 (reach it with an SSH tunnel). LAN opt-in (anyone on that network can then read
# your journal; never expose it to the internet): set JOURNAL_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0 AND list the name or IP you type
# into the browser in JOURNAL_ALLOWED_HOSTS, otherwise the Host check answers 421. See docs/PI.md.
# JOURNAL_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# JOURNAL_ALLOWED_HOSTS=raspberrypi,raspberrypi.local,192.168.1.50
